	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Ashenvale is the great forest of the {link:night-elves}night elves{/link}, a land of towering trees, silver lakes and white ruins in the north of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. It runs from the grey sea of the {link:the-zoram-strand}Zoram Strand{/link} in the west to the river that divides it from {link:azshara}Azshara{/link} in the east. {link:darkshore}Darkshore{/link} and {link:felwood}Felwood{/link} lie to the north, and the {link:stonetalon-mountains}Stonetalon Mountains{/link} and {link:the-barrens}The Barrens{/link} to the south. For ten thousand years the night elves have kept it as a sacred wood. It is sacred no longer only to them. The axes of the {link:horde}Horde{/link} ring in its eastern valleys, and the forest has become the oldest and bitterest battlefield between the elves and the orcs.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The trees of Ashenvale are older than any chronicle. Before the {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link}, cities of the elves stood along its western shore, and the city of {link:the-zoram-strand}Zoram{/link} looked out over the sea. When the {link:well-of-eternity}Well of Eternity{/link} was destroyed, the sea rose and swallowed Zoram, and the ruins of the old temples were left scattered through the woods: {link:the-ruins-of-ordil-aran}Ordil'Aran{/link}, {link:bathran-s-haunt}Bathran's Haunt{/link}, the {link:the-ruins-of-stardust}Ruins of Stardust{/link} and the city of {link:xavian}Xavian{/link} in the east. After the war the night elves settled in the shadow of {link:mount-hyjal}Mount Hyjal{/link} and gave themselves to the ways of {link:cenarius}Cenarius{/link} and the druids. While the druids slept in the {link:emerald-dream}Emerald Dream{/link}, the {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link} of {link:tyrande-whisperwind}Tyrande Whisperwind{/link} kept watch over the forest through the ages of the Long Vigil. No chronicle records when {link:astranaar}Astranaar{/link} or the other villages of the forest were first raised.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[Ashenvale has not known peace since the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}. The {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link} hold {link:astranaar}Astranaar{/link}, {link:maestra-s-post}Maestra's Post{/link}, {link:silverwind-refuge}Silverwind Refuge{/link} and {link:forest-song}Forest Song{/link}, but their ranks are thin and their roads long. The furbolgs of the {link:thistlefur-village}Thistlefur{/link} and the Foulweald, once friends of the elves, have been poisoned by a corruption that creeps down from {link:felwood}Felwood{/link}, and they fall upon every traveller. {link:satyrs}Satyrs{/link} hold {link:night-run}Night Run{/link}, {link:satyrnaar}Satyrnaar{/link} and {link:xavian}Xavian{/link}. The {link:naga}naga{/link} have come back to the drowned ruins of {link:the-zoram-strand}Zoram{/link}, and a cult of the {link:twilight-s-hammer}Twilight's Hammer{/link} gathers in the flooded halls of {link:blackfathom-deeps}Blackfathom Deeps{/link}. In the east, the orcs of the Warsong cut timber for the {link:horde}Horde{/link} under the guard of {link:splintertree-post}Splintertree Post{/link}. On the western coast they have raised a second outpost, {link:zoram-gar-outpost}Zoram'gar{/link}. The elves answer every felled tree with arrows, and each season the war between the two peoples spreads a little further into the woods.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The night elves.{/b} {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link}, druids and priestesses who hold the villages of the forest and fight to keep it whole.
• {b}The dryads.{/b} The daughters of {link:cenarius}Cenarius{/link} still dance in the glades of {link:raynewood-retreat}Raynewood Retreat{/link} and the {link:the-shrine-of-aessina}Shrine of Aessina{/link}.
• {b}The {link:horde}Horde{/link}.{/b} The orcs of the Warsong, with trolls, {link:tauren}tauren{/link} and goblins beside them, hold {link:splintertree-post}Splintertree Post{/link}, the lumber camps of the east and {link:zoram-gar-outpost}Zoram'gar Outpost{/link} on the coast.
• {b}The {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}.{/b} Apothecaries of the {link:undercity}Undercity{/link} have crept into the barrows and ruins of the elves.
• {b}The furbolgs.{/b} The {link:thistlefur-village}Thistlefur{/link} of the north and the Foulweald of the south, maddened, and the {link:bloodtooth-camp}Bloodtooth{/link}, who follow a savage king.
• {b}The satyrs.{/b} The Felmusk, Bleakheart and {link:xavian}Xavian{/link} satyrs worship demons in the ruined temples of the east.
• {b}The {link:naga}naga{/link}.{/b} The Wrathtail naga haunt the {link:the-zoram-strand}Zoram Strand{/link} and the waters of {link:blackfathom-deeps}Blackfathom{/link}.
• {b}The demons.{/b} Felguards and infernals still stalk the canyon where {link:mannoroth}Mannoroth{/link} fell.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}{link:the-drowned-city}The Drowned City{/link}.{/b} In the {link:great-sundering}Sundering{/link}, the sea took {link:the-zoram-strand}Zoram{/link}. Its rulers, its ring and its secrets sank with it.
• {b}The Long Vigil.{/b} For ten thousand years the {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link} guarded Ashenvale while the druids slept, and the forest grew deep and quiet.
• {b}The Coming of the {link:orcs}Orcs{/link}.{/b} In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link} the orcs of {link:grom-hellscream}Grom Hellscream{/link} came to Ashenvale to cut timber for their new home. The Sentinels struck back, and {link:cenarius}Cenarius{/link} himself rose to defend the forest. Grom and his warriors drank from a spring fouled by the blood of {link:mannoroth}Mannoroth{/link}, and in that fury they slew the demigod. Afterwards, in a canyon of the eastern forest, Grom slew Mannoroth and freed his people from the blood curse, but he died of his wounds.
• {b}Hyjal.{/b} At the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link}, elves, orcs and humans stood together against {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link}, and the Legion was broken. The alliance of that day did not outlive the victory.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} The {link:horde}Horde{/link} still cuts the trees of Ashenvale. The night elves have never accepted it.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Forest",
			text = [=[• The Tome of {link:the-howling-vale}Mel'Thandris{/link}, kept at a ruined shrine near the {link:felwood}Felwood{/link} border, is said to record events of import on its own leaves. No one understands how.
• A {link:furbolgs}furbolg{/link} named {link:krolg}Krolg{/link} lives alone by {link:mystral-lake}Mystral Lake{/link}. He speaks only to his own kind, and he blames the elves for the ruin of his people.
• The hunters of {link:splintertree-post}Splintertree{/link} tell of three great beasts of the forest: the bear {link:ursangous}Ursangous{/link}, the nightsaber {link:shadumbra}Shadumbra{/link} and the hippogryph {link:sharptalon}Sharptalon{/link}. To bring down all three is a test of any hunter's worth.
• The satyrs have stolen the Branch of {link:cenarius}Cenarius{/link} from the dryads, and the dryads have not forgiven it.]=],
		},
	},
})

